@startuml 05f-activity-node-join
title Arbitrary L2 node joins the federation (no redeploy of existing clusters)

skinparam defaultFontName Menlo
skinparam activity {
    BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
    BorderColor Black
    DiamondBackgroundColor #EEEEEE
}

|Operator|
start
:flash ivalice image onto new node's disk;
:edit /boot/firmware/ivalice-node.conf:
  NODE_ROLE=worker
  NODE_HOSTNAME=<new>
  NODE_IP=<static /24 ip>
  NODE_FEDERATION_BOOTSTRAP=https://dalmasca:8443/bootstrap
  NODE_FEDERATION_TOKEN=<pre-shared token>;
:power on;

|ivalice-firstboot.sh|
:read /boot/firmware/ivalice-node.conf;
:configure network, hostname;
:request shared munge key over HTTPS\n(bootstrap URL, pre-shared token);
if (bootstrap 200 OK?) then (yes)
    :install /etc/munge/munge.key (0400);
    :enable + start munge;
    :touch /var/lib/ivalice/federation-ready;
else (no)
    :fail firstboot with clear error;
    stop
endif

|Operator|
:append hostname + IP to the federation
Ansible inventory in Git:
  inventory/federation.yml;
:push / PR-merge;

|Ansible (scheduled or on-demand)|
:pull inventory;
:render slurm.conf NodeName + PartitionName
  from inventory;
:scp slurm.conf to all heads;
:run scontrol reconfigure on each head;

|slurmctld|
:register new node into federation;
:mark IDLE;

|Operator|
:sbatch a test job targeting the new node:
  sbatch -w <new> hostname;

if (job returns hostname within 60s?) then (yes)
    :node is operational in federation;
    stop
else (no)
    :inspect slurmd.log on new node;
    :troubleshoot munge, firewall, DNS;
    stop
endif

note right
  **No down time on existing clusters.**
  `scontrol reconfigure` is live; the new
  node slots into the existing partition
  without restarting slurmctld.
end note

note right
  **Decommission is the inverse:**
  remove from inventory → re-render slurm.conf
  → scontrol reconfigure. The node's historical
  job records stay in sacct; its artifacts stay
  in MinIO (content-addressed, cluster-agnostic).
end note

@enduml
